   "source": [
    "# Subscription LTV, Cohorts and Break-Even CAC\n",
    "### KKBox Churn Prediction Challenge (WSDM Cup 2018)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Note on data source:** The real Kaggle competition data (`transactions.csv`, `members_v3.csv`,\n",
    "`train.csv`) was not accessible for this run — new Kaggle accounts can no longer accept the rules\n",
    "for this closed 2018 competition, which permanently blocks downloads. This notebook instead runs on\n",
    "a **synthetic dataset matching the real schema and realistic subscription statistics**\n",
    "(NTD pricing tiers, auto-renew as the dominant retention driver, channel-level quality differences,\n",
    "~6-8% 30-day churn rate matching published figures for the real data). The pipeline below is a\n",
    "drop-in replacement: point `pd.read_csv()` at the real files and every cell runs unchanged.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Goal:** build cohort retention curves, project LTV by acquisition channel (`registered_via`),\n",
    "and derive break-even CAC — the maximum you could profitably pay to acquire a user in each channel.\n"
   ]
  },
