   "id": "a00b19f4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Building the Revenue Ledger\n",
    "\n",
    "Merge transactions onto member records so every payment carries its acquisition channel and\n",
    "registration date. From that we derive **cohort age** — months elapsed since registration at the\n",
    "time of each transaction — which is the x-axis for every curve in this notebook."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "ba4f1e69",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-30T16:29:34.249107Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-30T16:29:34.248889Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-30T16:29:34.565582Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-30T16:29:34.564632Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Users acquired per channel:\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "channel\n",
       "Organic/Web        15119\n",
       "App Store           8721\n",
       "Paid Social         7330\n",
       "Partner Bundle      5632\n",
       "Affiliate/Promo     3198\n",
       "Name: cohort_size, dtype: int64"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 3,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "ledger = txn.merge(members[[\"msno\", \"registration_init_time\", \"channel\", \"city\"]], on=\"msno\", how=\"left\")\n",
    "ledger = ledger.dropna(subset=[\"registration_init_time\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "ledger[\"age_start_month\"] = ((ledger[\"transaction_date\"] - ledger[\"registration_init_time\"]).dt.days // 30).clip(lower=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Cap the \"active until\" date at the data cutoff before computing age_end_month.\n",
    "# Without this, a long prepaid plan (e.g. 410 days) bought shortly before the cutoff has a\n",
    "# membership_expire_date far in the FUTURE relative to the cutoff, which would mark the user\n",
    "# \"active\" in age-buckets that haven't chronologically occurred yet by the cutoff - inconsistent\n",
    "# with how eligibility is defined below, and it produces a spurious retention spike at the\n",
    "# corresponding age (all channels showing >=100% retention at the same age).\n",
    "ledger[\"_active_until\"] = ledger[\"membership_expire_date\"].clip(upper=DATA_CUTOFF)\n",
    "ledger[\"age_end_month\"] = ((ledger[\"_active_until\"] - ledger[\"registration_init_time\"]).dt.days // 30).clip(lower=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "cohort_size = members.groupby(\"channel\")[\"msno\"].nunique().rename(\"cohort_size\").sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "print(\"Users acquired per channel:\")\n",
    "cohort_size\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a7b41210",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Cohort Retention Curves\n",
    "\n",
    "For a valid cohort curve, the denominator at each age must be restricted to users who've actually\n",
    "had *time* to reach that age by the data cutoff — otherwise recently-acquired users get counted as\n",
    "\"still eligible\" for ages they haven't lived through yet, and the curve is biased. We compute an\n",
    "**eligible cohort size** per (channel, age) pair to correct for this right-censoring."
   ]
  },
