   "source": [
    "## 5. LTV Curves by Channel\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key methodological point:** the LTV numerator must be restricted to the same eligible population\n",
    "as the denominator at every age. Naively summing all revenue collected at each age bucket (which\n",
    "mixes contributions from cohorts of very different maturity) and dividing by a shrinking eligible\n",
    "count would badly inflate the tail of the curve. Instead, for each user we cap their observable\n",
    "history at *their own* cohort age (registration to data cutoff), then average cumulative revenue\n",
    "only across users who've actually lived long enough to reach each age."
   ]
  },
